{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790481932,"nonce":"iOvwwv+gL+yrOlfSP5egn6cCsYw=","title":"Compiler: bounds versioning does not recognise while-form and non-counted loop headers","message":"bounds_version.rs versions a loop whose header phi steps by a positive\nconstant and whose header leaves on `i \u003c N` with N defined before the\nloop. Loops the speed kernels run hot that it refuses on shape\n(ZYNTAX_TRACE_BOUNDS_VERSION=1):\n\n- fannkuch: \"header compare is not a counted exit\" and \"bound or\n  counter is not i64 or varies\" (while loops over perm/count, bounds\n  that change inside the outer loop)\n- scimark FFT_transform_internal: \"header branch is not a compare\"\n  (the header branches on a phi or a combined condition)\n- FFT_bitreverse, zb_list_from_wide_i32: \"no unique preheader\"\n- library loops (zb_list_slice_*, zb_list_assign_slice_from_*): the\n  preheader chooses between two loop headers, which the pass reads as\n  an existing version test and refuses\n\nAlso left: indices of the form a*i + b with a != 1, the zext'd u8\ntable-lookup index of crypto_pyaes, decreasing counters, and loops that\nare not innermost. Each needs its own recogniser arm and precheck.","files":null}]}